WEBVTT

00:20.850 --> 00:26.820
If I was dreaming, how did I forget?

00:26.890 --> 00:30.660
It pulsed through me, frigid, shocked me

00:30.660 --> 00:32.300
Can I do, do?

00:32.960 --> 00:37.960
I want you next to me when I summon you

00:39.130 --> 00:42.970
Waiting close by, but you seem far off

00:42.970 --> 00:45.310
Na, na, na, knight

00:45.310 --> 00:48.480
The more beautiful the rose

00:48.480 --> 00:51.450
The more its thorns hurt

00:51.450 --> 00:54.720
Now that I'm strong

00:54.720 --> 00:59.720
My heart knows to protect that vow

01:00.720 --> 01:03.760
Let's meet in the dark of night

01:03.760 --> 01:06.830
Where you're waiting

01:06.830 --> 01:09.830
You'll worship the cruel Dark Queen

01:09.830 --> 01:13.000
Who's drunk with danger

01:13.000 --> 01:15.970
You shattered the glass sword

01:15.970 --> 01:18.940
You wielded without thinking

01:18.940 --> 01:21.880
Its shards glow in the night

01:21.880 --> 01:25.350
I lick your wounded fingers

01:54.680 --> 01:58.350
My, they're running late.

02:03.450 --> 02:07.520
They went out and still aren't back yet.

02:07.520 --> 02:10.120
Shall we go ahead and eat without them?

02:10.130 --> 02:12.090
They went out?

02:12.090 --> 02:14.010
On tonight of all nights?

02:22.800 --> 02:27.810
What's wrong? I told you to keep
an eye on the Princess.

02:32.910 --> 02:37.990
Oh, a lunar eclipse is approaching.

02:39.150 --> 02:43.030
I think it's best to stay in tonight.

02:57.340 --> 02:59.270
How's it look, Flandre?

02:59.270 --> 03:00.370
Huga.

03:00.380 --> 03:01.480
No good, huh?

03:01.480 --> 03:03.110
Hime!

03:03.580 --> 03:05.790
Take a look at this.

03:11.720 --> 03:14.420
A village, huh? It's pretty close.

03:14.420 --> 03:18.560
We might be able to find someone
who can fix the car there.

03:18.560 --> 03:21.700
It doesn't look like anyone's going to drive by.

03:22.760 --> 03:24.400
Flandre...

03:28.940 --> 03:29.940
Huga.

03:29.940 --> 03:31.750
Thank you.

03:33.640 --> 03:36.080
Th..Thanks.

03:36.080 --> 03:37.720
Huga.

03:51.660 --> 03:54.160
It's tough to get your footing here.

03:54.160 --> 03:55.970
Hime, be care...

04:01.240 --> 04:03.220
You're one to talk.

04:04.740 --> 04:09.350
My goodness, you fail as a soldier.

04:17.920 --> 04:20.130
Wait, Flandre.

04:26.960 --> 04:28.330
Flandre?

04:28.330 --> 04:30.140
Hime, Flandre, she...

04:34.440 --> 04:36.070
Hime!

04:50.890 --> 04:53.390
Ow, ow, ow...

04:59.930 --> 05:02.930
Ah! I..l..l..l..l..I'm sorry!

05:09.070 --> 05:10.710
Hime!

05:45.340 --> 05:48.750
This place seems pretty desolate.

05:59.720 --> 06:02.570
Looks like no one's here.

06:06.090 --> 06:11.090
Let's see, Akasabi Village...

06:11.970 --> 06:14.770
The village chief's wife has gone missing.

06:14.770 --> 06:18.110
Have they still not found the Chief's wife?

06:28.850 --> 06:32.630
Excuse me! Sorry to knock so late at night!

06:38.060 --> 06:42.060
H..Hime, you can't just barge in like that!

06:42.960 --> 06:45.300
They'll be angry when they get back!

06:45.300 --> 06:46.940
Geez...

06:47.940 --> 06:48.940
Huh?

06:48.940 --> 06:52.540
Don't worry, I'm not picking up any presence.

06:52.540 --> 06:55.350
Besides, I have to take care of my injury first.

07:00.550 --> 07:02.950
No presence?

07:02.950 --> 07:05.590
I'm not picking up the presence
of any living creatures.

07:05.590 --> 07:09.360
The village may be empty.

07:09.360 --> 07:11.090
They deserted it?

07:11.090 --> 07:12.660
Who knows.

07:12.660 --> 07:14.870
In any case, there's no need
to stay here any longer.

07:16.400 --> 07:18.840
I have a bad feeling about this place.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.210
What's wrong?

07:27.510 --> 07:30.080
There's another picture now.

07:30.080 --> 07:34.720
The body of the village chief's wife,
who had gone missing, was found, murdered.

07:35.120 --> 07:37.650
Is there something about that article?

07:37.650 --> 07:39.750
How brutal...

07:39.750 --> 07:40.960
When her body was found,

07:40.960 --> 07:44.990
her head appeared to have been
cut off with a sickle.

07:44.990 --> 07:48.670
And now the Director of the village
has gone missing.

07:54.600 --> 07:57.410
Someone was here just now, huh?

07:57.940 --> 07:59.510
Let's go, Hiro.

07:59.510 --> 08:03.220
It seems the bad feeling I was having
was absolutely correct.

08:18.060 --> 08:19.930
This is the same spot as before.

08:19.930 --> 08:21.600
Why?

08:21.600 --> 08:23.230
Hiro!

08:28.540 --> 08:30.380
No way...

08:31.270 --> 08:33.470
A third person.

08:33.480 --> 08:35.910
His head was cut off with a sickle.

08:35.910 --> 08:39.910
They said they found the Director's body
in the yard behind his house.

08:39.910 --> 08:42.550
What the heck is going on?

09:11.310 --> 09:13.120
What is it?

09:14.180 --> 09:16.750
Hime! There's a person's silhouette up there!

09:20.920 --> 09:23.100
Let's have a closer look.

09:35.070 --> 09:37.070
Is anyone home?

09:42.410 --> 09:46.120
H..Hime, you barged in again!

09:49.550 --> 09:52.120
Pardon me.

09:59.990 --> 10:02.130
As no one was able to identify
the suspect, the defendant was acquitted.

10:02.130 --> 10:03.430
No one's here.

10:04.370 --> 10:06.770
I'm sure I saw someone's silhouette before.

10:08.040 --> 10:10.200
I mean look, the TV is still on.

10:10.210 --> 10:13.940
Next, we will report on the disappearance
in Akasabi Village.

10:13.940 --> 10:18.150
According to the official autopsy conducted
on the two bodies that have been discovered,

10:18.150 --> 10:21.620
tne police believe the similiarities in the way
they were murdered points to a single suspect.

10:21.620 --> 10:25.090
Furthermore, the whereabouts
of the missing person are
unknown as yet,

10:25.090 --> 10:27.420
and the police do not know if he is dead or alive.

10:27.420 --> 10:29.660
My goodness...

10:29.660 --> 10:33.930
The entire village has gone quiet now,
it creeps me out.

10:33.930 --> 10:37.640
Damn, who is behind the murders?
Do you think it's him? Or maybe...

10:41.140 --> 10:46.140
So far, the police have determined that all the victims are involved
with the construction site of a dam.

10:46.140 --> 10:46.940
Before, I said no one is in this village.

10:46.940 --> 10:49.080
Before, I said no one is in this village.

10:49.080 --> 10:50.080
The three consective murders have
the local residents nervous for their safety.

10:50.080 --> 10:54.010
Besides the absence of people,
the village itself seems suspicious.

10:54.020 --> 10:58.260
They pray that the suspect is apprehended at
once to save any further victims.

11:27.450 --> 11:29.790
A village that doesn't exist?

11:33.050 --> 11:34.720
Look at the date.

11:34.720 --> 11:36.530
The date?

11:37.960 --> 11:41.700
August 11th, 1965?

11:41.700 --> 11:43.900
Over forty years ago?!

11:46.630 --> 11:49.640
The items on the bulletin board keep changing.

11:49.640 --> 11:51.710
Every time we pass by it.

11:52.340 --> 11:55.340
The number of photos of missing
people has increased!

11:55.340 --> 11:57.880
So, there's a fourth victim now.

11:57.880 --> 12:00.860
Then, those crosses...

12:01.050 --> 12:05.090
...have to do with the string of disappearances
we saw on the news?!

12:05.090 --> 12:08.400
The proper term is "serial murders".

12:09.160 --> 12:13.130
The fourth victim was the Chief's only son.

12:13.430 --> 12:16.560
Even the date on the article has been updated.

12:16.560 --> 12:18.640
Now it says August 14th.

12:18.830 --> 12:23.000
That means three days have passed
since we left the house.

12:23.000 --> 12:25.240
We don't have time for this!

12:25.240 --> 12:27.510
Let's get the heck out of this village!

12:27.510 --> 12:29.510
That's impossible.

12:29.510 --> 12:33.120
I don't know why, but we were unable
to find the way out before.

12:40.150 --> 12:42.000
Then that means...

12:44.290 --> 12:46.830
Listen well to what I'm about to say.

12:47.960 --> 12:52.960
You're the only soldier I have to protect me
in this closed space.

12:53.170 --> 12:58.170
I will not allow you to leave my side
from this moment on.

12:58.170 --> 12:59.870
Understood?

12:59.870 --> 13:01.790
Y..Yes...

13:16.660 --> 13:18.490
No way!

13:18.490 --> 13:21.400
The Chief's son was murdered.

13:21.400 --> 13:23.840
What the hell are the police doing?

13:33.610 --> 13:37.610
We can't rely on the police any more!

13:37.610 --> 13:40.960
Let's find the suspect ourselves!

13:41.620 --> 13:45.030
Hime, something's not right.

13:45.790 --> 13:50.190
It seems we're living through
someone else's memories.

13:50.190 --> 13:55.440
But not a person's,
the memories of the village itself.

13:56.100 --> 13:58.600
The memories of the village itself?!

13:58.600 --> 14:00.600
Wh..What?

14:00.600 --> 14:02.340
Hiro...

14:18.120 --> 14:19.590
What is it this time?

14:19.590 --> 14:20.990
Serves you right!

14:20.990 --> 14:24.990
He was the only one who kept going
against the Chief!

14:24.990 --> 14:29.700
Why must we be fated to die
along with this village?

15:02.200 --> 15:04.140
No way...

15:14.310 --> 15:15.910
That's...

15:15.910 --> 15:17.720
He. S comin Q!

15:56.620 --> 15:58.260
Hey!

16:09.100 --> 16:11.480
You don't run away from an opponent like that.

16:12.270 --> 16:15.940
Come on! He showed up out of nowhere,
and even you...

16:15.940 --> 16:21.720
Certainly, I'm in no condition to be fighting
and I'd just slow you down.

16:22.310 --> 16:24.090
Pathetic.

16:25.080 --> 16:26.650
Don't say that.

16:26.650 --> 16:28.820
It's written on the board.

16:28.820 --> 16:29.350
Fire in Akasabi Village

16:29.350 --> 16:32.620
That fire from before was arson by the villagers.

16:32.620 --> 16:34.020
Arson?

16:34.020 --> 16:37.230
It seems there was a plan to build a dam
where the village was located.

16:37.730 --> 16:42.460
The ones who disappeared and were killed
were all supporters of the dam.

16:42.460 --> 16:46.430
Naturally, people were suspicious of
the opposition group's leader.

16:47.030 --> 16:50.020
So, that man from before was
in the opposition group?

16:50.640 --> 16:53.410
Their suspicions were correct,

16:53.410 --> 16:57.140
but he went mad and massacred the lot of them.

16:57.150 --> 16:59.250
That's terrible...

17:00.110 --> 17:01.580
Don't worry about it.

17:01.580 --> 17:04.690
We can't do anything about the past.

17:06.720 --> 17:11.720
Residents of Akasabi Village, they're about to begin the flow
of water to the dam.

17:13.460 --> 17:15.100
Hime!

17:16.530 --> 17:21.530
It's very regrettable that we were
unable to stop the plan.

17:22.040 --> 17:26.270
Our forefathers resided in this village.

17:26.270 --> 17:30.410
Our grandfathers, our grandmothers, they were all raised in this village.

17:30.410 --> 17:31.580
It's him.

17:31.580 --> 17:38.220
Therefore, don't you agree we should accept death along with the village?

17:42.590 --> 17:43.660
Water?!

17:43.660 --> 17:45.960
Seems we're going along for the ride.

17:45.960 --> 17:47.360
No way...

17:47.360 --> 17:49.430
What should we do?

17:50.160 --> 17:55.380
You're the only soldier I have to protect me
in this closed space.

17:56.570 --> 17:59.370
No, I have to get it together.

17:59.370 --> 18:02.380
I don't have Flandre or Liza with me.

18:02.810 --> 18:05.090
There's only me.

18:05.680 --> 18:08.680
I have to protect Hime.

18:08.680 --> 18:10.280
I'll go look for a way out!

18:10.280 --> 18:12.190
I told you not to leave my side.

18:12.190 --> 18:13.450
But!

18:13.450 --> 18:15.420
He's a reckless murderer.

18:15.420 --> 18:18.460
I'm positive he'll come and try to kill us.

18:18.460 --> 18:20.230
B..But...

18:20.230 --> 18:21.870
However,

18:24.670 --> 18:27.610
it would be prudent to move someplace else.

19:27.430 --> 19:29.070
Hime...

20:32.130 --> 20:34.570
Are you all right, Hime?

20:39.030 --> 20:40.880
I guess.

20:48.310 --> 20:52.680
I wonder if we'll be able to go back to our world?

20:52.680 --> 20:54.490
Who knows.

21:14.270 --> 21:15.910
Huga.

21:16.500 --> 21:18.140
Flandre...

21:19.110 --> 21:20.810
Wh..Where's Hime?!

21:20.810 --> 21:22.620
Right here.

21:23.280 --> 21:24.920
Hime!

21:28.580 --> 21:30.530
Where's Akasabi Village?

21:37.660 --> 21:40.630
What the hell happened yesterday?

21:40.630 --> 21:42.270
Huga.

21:42.560 --> 21:45.060
Huga, huga, huga.

21:45.070 --> 21:46.970
I see.

21:46.970 --> 21:52.540
It appears we were pulled into the village's tragic
memories during the witching hour.

21:52.770 --> 21:54.810
I'm not sure I follow,

21:55.740 --> 21:57.420
but I'm glad we're safe.

21:57.950 --> 22:00.620
Yeah, you did well.

22:13.060 --> 22:18.060
Get down on your knees and lick my red nails

22:18.630 --> 22:26.570
Call me queen with your entangled tongue

22:29.140 --> 22:31.910
The sun that blooms in Hell

22:31.910 --> 22:34.650
Darkness that's fallen to Paradise

22:34.650 --> 22:37.220
If you're confronted with light and despair

22:37.220 --> 22:39.850
Which one goes deeper?

22:39.850 --> 22:42.590
Roses fly from my head

22:42.590 --> 22:45.290
I'll scatter them into Nirvana

22:45.290 --> 22:47.890
Wounds that secretly pain you

22:47.900 --> 22:50.470
Blood that gushes away

22:50.530 --> 22:53.170
They both lead to the depths of my heart

22:53.170 --> 22:55.840
You've given these gorgeous gifts as tribute

22:55.840 --> 22:58.510
And yet you're still

22:58.510 --> 23:01.210
Seeking love?

23:01.210 --> 23:03.940
Tell me exactly to what extent

23:03.940 --> 23:06.610
Grown men are just foolish little boys?

23:06.610 --> 23:11.610
Get down on your knees and lick my sacred feet

23:11.890 --> 23:16.890
Call me queen in your hoarse voice

23:17.320 --> 23:22.320
The proof of your life creeps up the tower of pain

23:22.560 --> 23:25.270
Slowly making your way, you can barely breathe

23:25.270 --> 23:27.900
But if you still ask for it

23:27.900 --> 23:31.870
Your dying breath just might be

23:31.870 --> 23:40.160
The words that melt my frozen tears

23:41.850 --> 23:43.050
Huga.

23:43.050 --> 23:44.550
Pinch our pennies!

23:44.550 --> 23:45.890
Eat lightly!

23:45.890 --> 23:48.120
Don't leave the refrigerator door open for long!

23:48.120 --> 23:50.190
Don't let the faucet run!

23:50.190 --> 23:52.430
Turn off electrical appliances
when you aren't using them!

23:52.430 --> 23:55.460
Come on, Liza, idle reduction!

23:55.460 --> 23:58.000
What are you doing, Hiro?

23:58.000 --> 24:01.400
Next episode, we live frugally!
"Princess Frugality"

24:01.400 --> 24:02.170
Wrong.

24:02.800 --> 24:04.240
Huh? Oh, my mistake!

24:04.240 --> 24:06.410
Next episode, "Princess Dead Sprint"

24:06.410 --> 24:07.870
Don't try jokes that are hard to understand, Hiro.

24:09.280 --> 24:10.780
Huga, huga.
